BEGIN:VCALENDAR
BEGIN:VJOURNAL
CONCEPT:semcal:concept:note
SUMMARY:Reasons why iCalendar is good for interoperability
STYLED-DESCRIPTION;VALUE=TEXT;FMTTYPE=text/markdown:\n
 1. Human-readable text - even if you don't support full parsing you can understand the content and use text processing
  tools like grep, awk, etc. to extract values;\n
 2. Common semantics for standardized properties - data is meaningful without needing to know the source;\n
 3. Compatibility is assured via graceful degradation - specifications explicitly state how unrecognized data is to
  be handled;\n
 4. Most email clients also support iCalendar events - so you can email data to almost anyone and benefit from
  existing calendar features;
 5. Object linking support allows for building knowledge graphs;
DESCRIPTION;DERIVED=TRUE:\n
 1. Human-readable text - even if you don't support full parsing you can understand the content and use text processing
  tools like grep to extract values;\n
 2. Common semantics for standardized properties - data is meaningful without needing to know the source;\n
 3. Compatibility is assured via graceful degradation - specifications explicitly state how unrecognized data is to
  be handled;\n
END:VJOURNAL
END:VCALENDAR
